# fmt: on
"""The nearest ANSI (0-15) color for each ANSI256 (0-255) color, by CIEDE2000.

Generated from a nearest-neighbour search over the 16 base colors. That search
reads only `ANSI_HEX_CODES`, which is fixed, so each of the 256 answers is
fixed too, but computing one at runtime cost 16 CIEDE2000 distances, each
converting both operands through linear RGB, XYZ and L*a*b*.

termenv runs this search with the HSLuv distance. HSLuv rates pale colors as
highly saturated, so tints such as #ffd7d7 degraded to vivid red rather than
white; CIEDE2000 tracks perceived difference instead.

To regenerate: for each `value` in 0..255, take the `index` in 0..15 that
minimises `Color.rgb(ANSI_HEX_CODES[value]).distance_ciede2000(Color.rgb(ANSI_HEX_CODES[index]))`,
resolving ties toward the lower index as a linear scan does.
"""


